---
import '@fontsource/sora/400.css';
import '@fontsource/sora/600.css';
import '../../styles/analytics-reports.css';
import '../../styles/competitor-gaps.css';
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"/><title>Competitor Gap Finder | NC Digital</title></head><body>
<header><a class="brand" href="/admin/links/">NC <span>Digital</span></a><nav><a href="/admin/keyword-research/">Keyword research</a><a href="/admin/links/">All tools ↗</a></nav></header>
<main><div class="intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">COMPETITOR RESEARCH · DIRECT BUSINESSES ONLY</p><h1>Find the gaps.<br/><span>Decide what to build next.</span></h1><p>Compare your client with up to three competitors. Find overlooked keywords, weaker rankings and practical page opportunities.</p></div><div class="connection"><p id="connection">Checking DataForSEO…</p><p id="daily"></p></div></div>
<section class="panel setup"><form id="form"><fieldset id="fields"><div class="form-grid"><label>Client website<input id="client" required placeholder="yourclient.co.uk" maxlength="1000" autocomplete="off"/></label><label>Direct competitor websites<textarea id="competitors" required rows="3" maxlength="3000" placeholder="competitor-one.co.uk&#10;competitor-two.co.uk&#10;competitor-three.co.uk"></textarea><small>One per line. Known directories and platforms are blocked.</small></label></div><details class="refinements"><summary>Focus, exclusions and spending controls</summary><div class="form-grid"><label>Focus phrases — match any<input id="focus" maxlength="350" placeholder="Optional: plumber, boiler, heating"/><small>Up to five comma-separated phrases. Use a town name to narrow the keyword wording.</small></label><label>Exclude brand terms<input id="brands" maxlength="1200" placeholder="Optional: client name, competitor brand"/><small>Filters returned keywords without additional paid requests.</small></label><label>Rows per lookup<select id="limit"><option value="50">50 · smaller shortlist</option><option value="100" selected>100 · standard</option><option value="200">200 · broader shortlist</option></select></label><label>Minimum UK monthly searches<input id="volume" type="number" value="10" min="0" max="100000"/></label><label>Competitor ranking range<select id="rank"><option value="10">Top 10</option><option value="20" selected>Top 20</option><option value="50">Top 50</option><option value="100">Top 100</option></select></label><label>Run spending allowance (USD)<input id="budget" type="number" min="0.05" max="2" step="0.05" value="0.50"/></label></div><label class="checkbox refresh"><input id="fresh" type="checkbox"/> Refresh cached comparisons</label></details><div class="form-footer"><p>UK · English · organic rankings. Search volumes are UK estimates, not town-level totals.</p><button id="preview" class="primary" disabled>Preview comparison ↗</button></div></fieldset></form><div id="quote" hidden><div><strong id="quote-title"></strong><p id="quote-copy"></p></div><button id="start" class="primary">Start comparison ↗</button></div></section>
<p id="notice" class="notice" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></p>
<details class="panel directory-settings"><summary>Directory exclusions <span id="excluded-count"></span></summary><p>Yell, Checkatrade, MyBuilder and other known directories are excluded, including their subdomains. Add any other directory here to block it from future lookups and saved report results.</p><form id="exclude-form"><label>Directory domain<input id="exclude-domain" placeholder="directory-example.co.uk" maxlength="1000" required/></label><button>Exclude directory</button></form><p id="custom-exclusions"></p></details>
<div class="saved"><label for="saved">Saved comparisons</label><select id="saved"><option value="">Choose a report…</option></select><button id="open">Open report</button></div>
<section id="progress" class="panel" hidden><div class="progress-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">COMPARISON IN PROGRESS</p><h2 id="phase"></h2><p id="progress-copy"></p></div><div><button id="resume" hidden>Resume</button><button id="stop">Stop</button></div></div></section>
<section id="empty" class="empty"><span>RESEARCH → EVIDENCE → PAGE PLAN</span><h2>Put competitor research to work.</h2><p>Start with businesses offering the same services to the same customers. A relevant local competitor usually provides a more useful comparison than a large national directory.</p><div class="features"><article><h3>Not observed for your client</h3><p>Queries where a competitor appears in the provider’s data but the client is not observed.</p></article><article><h3>Rankings to improve</h3><p>Shared queries where a competitor is at least three organic positions ahead.</p></article><article><h3>Control the spend</h3><p>Preview the allowance, reuse 30-day lookup caches and see confirmed charges after the run.</p></article></div></section>
<article id="report" hidden><div class="report-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">NC DIGITAL · COMPETITOR GAP REPORT</p><h2 id="title"></h2><p id="scope"></p><p id="cost"></p></div><div class="report-actions"><button id="export">Export shortlist</button><button id="print" class="primary">Print page plan</button></div></div><div id="warnings"></div><div id="stats" class="gap-stats"></div>
<nav class="gap-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Report views"><button role="tab" id="keywords-tab" aria-controls="keywords-panel" aria-selected="true" data-tab="keywords">Keyword opportunities</button><button role="tab" id="plans-tab" aria-controls="plans-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" data-tab="plans">Suggested page plan</button><button role="tab" id="coverage-tab" aria-controls="coverage-panel" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" data-tab="coverage">Coverage & spend</button></nav>
<section id="keywords-panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="keywords-tab"><div class="filters"><input id="search" type="search" placeholder="Filter keywords…" aria-label="Filter keywords"/><select id="type" aria-label="Opportunity type"><option value="all">All opportunities</option><option value="missing">Client not observed</option><option value="improve">Improve existing ranking</option></select><select id="status-filter" aria-label="Work status"><option value="active">Active work</option><option value="all">All statuses</option><option value="done">Done</option><option value="dismissed">Dismissed</option></select><select id="sort" aria-label="Sort shortlist"><option value="score">Sort: priority</option><option value="volume">Sort: volume</option><option value="difficulty">Sort: difficulty</option></select><span id="count"></span></div><p class="muted">“Not observed” is a database finding, not proof that a page is absent or unindexed. Click Inspect to see the ranking URLs and evidence.</p><div class="table-panel"><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Keyword / suggested action</th><th>UK searches</th><th>Difficulty</th><th>Your rank</th><th>Best competitor</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody id="rows"></tbody></table></div><p id="no-results" hidden>No opportunities match these filters.</p></div></section>
<section id="plans-panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="plans-tab" hidden><p class="muted">Draft page ideas group related keywords using the observed URLs. Confirm search intent and the client’s services before commissioning content. Keywords should not automatically become separate pages.</p><div id="plans" class="gap-plans"></div></section>
<section id="coverage-panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="coverage-tab" hidden><div id="coverage"></div><div id="ledger"></div></section>
<footer class="methodology"><h3>How this shortlist is produced</h3><p>Each competitor has two bounded lookups: keywords where only the competitor is observed, and shared keywords. Shared opportunities require a competitor to be at least three organic positions ahead. Results are not a live local rank check and exclude paid ads and map-pack positions.</p><p>Monthly volume is a UK estimate and is not added across similar keywords or competitors. CPC is in USD and describes advertising, not job value. Keyword difficulty is a provider estimate, not a guarantee. Priority combines volume, the number of competitors, position gaps, intent and difficulty; it is a sorting heuristic.</p><p>The provider’s database can be incomplete, especially for small local sites. Snapshots may differ in date. Related-page suggestions use title/path word overlap and have not been verified by crawling the whole site. Saved comparisons are reused for seven days and individual lookups for 30 days unless refreshed.</p><p>Each uncached lookup reserves $0.05 USD before dispatch. Unknown charges remain reserved and matching requests are not automatically repeated for 24 hours. The rolling daily allowance is $2 across this tool. Provider pricing changes can exceed an estimate; if detected, further paid calls stop.</p><p><a href="https://docs.dataforseo.com/v3/dataforseo_labs-google-domain_intersection-live/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DataForSEO source and data coverage ↗</a></p></footer></article></main>
<dialog id="detail"><div class="dialog-heading"><p class="eyebrow">RANKING EVIDENCE & NEXT ACTION</p><button id="close" aria-label="Close details">✕</button></div><div id="detail-body"></div><form id="task-form"><label>Work status<select id="task-status"><option value="to-do">To do</option><option value="in-progress">In progress</option><option value="done">Done</option><option value="dismissed">Dismissed</option></select></label><label>Planned work / notes<textarea id="task-notes" rows="4" maxlength="3000"></textarea></label><button id="save-task" class="primary">Save work item</button><span id="task-message" role="status"></span></form></dialog><script>import '../../scripts/competitor-gaps.js';</script></body></html>
